      <pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:08:26 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>Several major F1 broadcasters are reportedly opting against sending their television crews to the Qatar Grand Prix due to ongoing tensions in the Middle East. Sky Sports Germany will broadcast remotely from Munich, while ServusTV, Canal+ and DAZN Spain are also expected to be absent from the circuit. Sky Sports F1 (UK) and Viaplay will maintain their on-site coverage, while Sky Sport Italy’s plans remain unclear. Some broadcasters are still assessing their plans for Abu Dhabi, although a full media presence is currently expected.</description>
